  "causalModel": {
   "founding": "Rebuilt after the Slaughter of 4E 48 on the best natural harbour of the south coast, smaller and lower than the city it replaced.",
   "siteAdvantages": "The firm shelf at the head of the estuary, with the stilt quarters and the lighter quay stepping down off it into tidal water. Big hulls anchor out in Oliis Bay and lighter in. The lightering is the city's living.",
   "occupantsMotive": "A reconstituted merchant council governs by tariff; it will not appoint a ruler. The last party that had one killed the city.",
   "pressures": "Hostile to the An-Xileel successor state and indispensable to a bay that must trade somewhere. It is also built over its own mass grave.",
   "wouldChangeIf": "If the third Hist ever spoke to one faction alone, every institution here would break at once. The rules forbid it."
  },
